          "title": "Hanabi",
          "subtitle": "Matching",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Hanabi is a cooperative commercial card game where players hold their cards facing outward and give limited clues to build firework sequences."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Designed by Antoine Bauza, Hanabi is a modern cooperative card game known for hidden self-information: each player can see everyone elses cards but not their own."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "2-5 players use the table arrangement described for Hanabi."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Dedicated Hanabi firework card deck"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Dedicated Hanabi firework card deck, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Prepare the dedicated Hanabi deck and any shared scoring, resource, or tableau area described by the rules."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
